## 3. LeetCode 113 – Path Sum II

**Concepts:** DFS, Backtracking, Root-to-Leaf Path

**Approach:** Explore every root-to-leaf path. Store the path when its sum equals the target.

```java
class Solution {
    public List<List<Integer>> pathSum(TreeNode root, int targetSum) {
        List<List<Integer>> result = new ArrayList<>();
        List<Integer> path = new ArrayList<>();

        findPaths(root, targetSum, 0, path, result);
        return result;
    }

    private void findPaths(TreeNode node, int targetSum,
                           int sum, List<Integer> path,
                           List<List<Integer>> result) {
        if (node == null) return;

        path.add(node.val);
        sum += node.val;

        if (node.left == null && node.right == null
                && sum == targetSum) {
            result.add(new ArrayList<>(path));
        } else {
            findPaths(node.left, targetSum, sum, path, result);
            findPaths(node.right, targetSum, sum, path, result);
        }

        path.remove(path.size() - 1);
    }
}
```

**Time:** O(n + total output size)  
**Space:** O(h) auxiliary space, excluding the result.

